TrueNas Presentation

What is a NAS 
  NAS means Network Attache Storage
  It usually refers to a device that is meant solely for storage, just like a google drive

What's TrueNas ?
  TrueNas is a Linux based Operating System made to create and manage a NAS device.
  It can be installed on any x32-64 x86 or ARM device to make it into a special server, that you can tailor to your needs.
  The OS is quite light, making it a pretty good choice for older hardware, which means if you have an older computer that's 
been sitting around, it could be time to put it to good use !
  TrueNas has been mainly used to create storage servers, In my case, I putted it on a second hand computer for my family, 
to which I added two 2To HDD in a mirror configuration
  But it can be used and configured for many other uses, just like any linux distribution.

Going beyond a simple storage server ?
  TrueNas supports Docker, which is a really usefull tool to compartmentalize services, like webservers or databases.
  You can directly install apps on it, for instance, one very handy application was Tailscale a VPN, making any device connected to my
tailscale able to connect to the server
